From 04cb9799c24eb3453c2591e05b9b3d82aaa0ab16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 16:30:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 34/75] frameworks/base: add microG signature spoofing (0026)
 on AOSP-13

Maintained variant: applied lineageos4microg/docker-lineage-cicd
signature_spoofing_patches/android_frameworks_base-Android13.patch
(applies clean), rather than hand-porting the AOSP-11 0026 -- 13 moved
generatePackageInfo from PackageManagerService to ComputerEngine
(PackageStateInternal ps, long flags), and the upstream patch also
carries a fix the 11 patch lacked: OR-in requestsFakeSignature so
FAKE_PACKAGE_SIGNATURE lands in the computed permission set even without
GET_PERMISSIONS.

Adds android.permission.FAKE_PACKAGE_SIGNATURE (dangerous) +
android.permission-group.FAKE_PACKAGE, and ComputerEngine.mayFakeSignature
rewrites PackageInfo.signatures for apps that declare a "fake-signature"
meta-data and hold the permission (targetSdk > LOLLIPOP_MR1), wrapped in
a Throwable catch.

fydroid enhancements on top of upstream:
- Also spoof pi.signingInfo (GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES, P+) via
  new SigningInfo(new SigningDetails(Signature[], SignatureSchemeVersion.JAR,
  null, null)) -- SigningDetails is top-level android.content.pm in 13.
  microG GmsCore >= 2024-12-12 self-checks signingInfo, so spoofing only
  pi.signatures is insufficient.
- config_locationProviderPackageNames += com.google.android.gms for
  microG's network location provider.

api/current.txt regenerated via `m update-api` (not hand-merged). Builds
clean (m services framework-minus-apex framework-res, EXIT 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
